WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.537
How well the desk is staffed shows up in
its numbers before it shows up in an audit.

2
00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.562
Each measure says something specific.

3
00:00:06.562 --> 00:00:09.500
Tickets past their service
level show capacity.

4
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:13.175
A rising escalation share
shows gaps in the runbooks.

5
00:00:13.175 --> 00:00:16.850
Tickets sent back for missing
evidence show slipping discipline.

6
00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:19.594
Privileged elevations
with no matching ticket

7
00:00:19.594 --> 00:00:22.063
mean the queue and the
roles have come apart.

8
00:00:22.063 --> 00:00:25.000
And work done outside the
front door is a side door.

9
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.987
Each problem has a different fix: more
people, a better runbook, or training.

10
00:00:29.987 --> 00:00:34.201
The platform produces the numbers,
so nobody reports on their own work.

11
00:00:34.201 --> 00:00:39.562
The decision for the CIO: staff and source
the desk from these measures, monthly.

12
00:00:39.562 --> 00:00:41.350
Next, the change board.
